# Deliberately carries no `version` or `date-released`. Those would be a fourth
# version surface for the release flow to keep in step with pyproject.toml,
# plugin.yaml and dashboard/manifest.json — and the one nobody would remember
# to bump. The fields here are the ones that do not change between releases.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hermes Talk in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Hermes Talk"
abstract: >-
  A realtime voice plugin for Hermes Agent. One bidirectional speech-to-speech
  session in which the agent uses its real tools, takes interruption, delegates
  background work while you keep talking, and speaks results when they land.
  Runs in the terminal, in a Discord voice channel and in the Hermes dashboard.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "SmokeDev"
    alias: "TheSmokeDev"
    website: "https://github.com/TheSmokeDev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheSmokeDev/hermes-talk"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/hermes-talk/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - hermes-talk
  - hermes-agent
  - voice
  - realtime
  - speech-to-speech
  - voice-agent
  - plugin
  - python
